 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Developer diagnostics
+
+The homepage has independent, user-initiated browser connection checks for a private
+Wi-Fi device and a loopback companion CLI. Replace the example URLs with your
+services' read-only health endpoints; no particular CLI or device API is assumed.
+A successful HTTP 2xx response verifies reachability at that moment. No service
+requests run on page load, and no application-server proxy is involved.
+
+Serve the site over HTTPS (localhost is also a secure context). Services must allow
+the site's origin via `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`. The device must listen on its
+LAN interface; the CLI should bind to loopback. Requests omit credentials and use
+`targetAddressSpace: 'local'` for the device and `'loopback'` for the CLI. Browser
+network permissions and HTTP mixed-content support vary; see the
+[Chrome Local Network Access guide](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance/guides/security/local-network-access).
+The widget provides permission, CORS, and connectivity troubleshooting inline.
+
+Run the isolated connection helper checks with Node 22.18+:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/diagnostics.test.mjs
+```
